 :bonsai-admission-contracts
 {:cmd ["sh" "-c" "ulimit -s 65520; node --stack-size=60000 --max-old-space-size=8192 \"$(command -v nbb)\" --classpath \"$(kbb -Spath -M:verify-admissions):../text/src\" os/aiueos/scripts/verify-admissions.cljk os/aiueos/contracts/qwen35-gguf-header-valid-v1.edn os/aiueos/contracts/qwen35-gguf-kv-scan-v1.edn os/aiueos/contracts/qwen35-tensor-table-bind-v1.edn"]
  :doc "Bonsai stage A item 3 (ADR-0222): the THREE two-profile admission objects executed in the KIR oracle over the REAL Bonsai header (bonsai-admission-fixture): header-valid 11 vectors; kv-scan 15 vectors including the admitted 144-byte workspace computed independently, both profile mix-ups, and one refusal per Prism key; tensor-table-bind 12 vectors including the admitted 28,160-byte workspace (851 binding slots) also computed independently, the profile mix-up, and one mutation per refusal class. SLOW: every kv-scan full-walk vector visits 495,907 length-prefixed token/merge strings in the interpreter (~32 min for that contract; the tensor table is ~100 s); see the contracts for the measured times. The Qwen3.8 profile's evidence stays the JVM parity tests."}

 :bonsai-admission-native
 {:cmd ["sh" "-c" "set -eu; AMU=${AMU:-../amu}; K=os/aiueos/kotoba; T=$(mktemp -d); for o in qwen35-gguf-header-valid:kotoba_aiueos_qwen35_gguf_header_valid qwen35-gguf-kv-scan:kotoba_aiueos_qwen35_gguf_kv_scan qwen35-tensor-table-bind:kotoba_aiueos_qwen35_tensor_table_bind; do n=${o%%:*}; sym=${o#*:}; \"$AMU/bin/amu\" compile $K/$n.kotoba --target x86_64-aiueos-kernel-v1 --output $T/$n.o --jvm-free > /dev/null; cmp $T/$n.o $K/$n.o; python3 os/aiueos/scripts/verify-kotoba-kernel-object.py $K/$n.o \"\" $sym; done; echo AIUEOS_BONSAI_ADMISSION_NATIVE_OK objects=3"]
  :doc "Bonsai stage A item 3 (ADR-0222): the three two-profile admission objects COMPILE with the pinned amu (single-file --jvm-free, their recorded recipe), are byte-identical to the committed .o, and pass the ABI verifier. The kv-scan key tables are balanced comparison trees because a 113-deep if chain -- the previous table -- no longer compiles with amu b36eb717 (desugared nesting exhausted the host stack). AMU defaults to ../amu."}

 :bonsai-c-translation
 {:cmd ["kbb" "--backend" "sci" "os/aiueos/scripts/smoke-bonsai-runtime-translation.cljk"]
  :doc "Bonsai stage A item 3 (ADR-0222), the C half: `aiueos_qwen35_model_translate` compiled alone (-DAIUEOS_QWEN35_KOTOBA_ADMISSION -DAIUEOS_QWEN35_TRANSLATION_ONLY) is handed the Bonsai profile's two workspaces -- the 144-byte and 28,160-byte `:expect-plan-hex` of the kv-scan and tensor-table contracts, which bonsai-admission-contracts pins to what the objects produce -- and must build the struct contracts/bonsai2-qwen35-runtime-v1.edn describes: 851 records into 851 fields with the contract's dimensions and ggml types, the histogram in the counter slots (PTQ1_0 143 counts in slot 31), the extents still tiling the artifact after the offset subtraction, and layer 64 untouched because this artifact has no MTP head. TWO walks in opposite directions: shapes against the graph contract, and every workspace record against the field its role id names (the ids are decoded from the object's own literal tables, because ffn_gate and ffn_up have the same shape and only the name tells them apart). Ten controls: one corrupted record the shape walk must NAME, and nine refusals whose reason literal is asserted (-103, -105, -106 x2, -107..-111). Host cc, no artifact and no QEMU: the translation never dereferences the model bytes. Exit 3 when no C compiler."}

 :bonsai-boot-fixture
 {:cmd ["kbb" "--backend" "sci" "os/aiueos/tests/make-bonsai-boot-fixture.cljk"]
  :pass-args? true
  :doc "Bonsai stage A (ADR-0222): the boot fixture for the Bonsai profile, which had none -- the QEMU admission smoke only has the 10,996,640-byte Qwen3.8 prefix that tests/make_qwen35_header_fixture.py synthesises, so the Bonsai admission has never been on a CPU. The fixture is NOT synthesised: it is the real, sha256-pinned 11,120,992-byte metadata + tensor-table prefix `bonsai-admission-fixture` range-fetches, the same bytes the three admission objects were graded over, so the boot does not run on a second header nothing else has read (ADR-0165). What the generator adds is the independent arm: a walk of those bytes that derives -- from the file, against contracts/bonsai2-qwen35-runtime-v1.edn -- the metadata end, the 28,672 INT32 signs (read SIGNED, and cross-checked against slots 128/132 of the workspace the kv-scan object produced), the 851 records with role, dimensions and ggml type, the 48/16 schedule against full_attention_interval, the type histogram, and the extents tiling to exactly 5,946,648,928 bytes; it writes the fixture and a receipt of every number the boot gate will assert. Ten controls, each refused by its own reason literal (:not-gguf :gguf-version :tensor-count :metadata-count :sign-value-not-unit :sign-values-count :unknown-role :role-dimensions :role-type :extent-not-contiguous). ~0.5 s, offline once the prefix is on disk; exit 3 (not 1) when it is not. Proves nothing about a boot: the CPU is the next floor."}

 :bonsai-ptq1-fused-arms
 {:cmd ["sh" "-c" "AMU=${AMU:-../amu}; exec kbb --backend sci os/aiueos/scripts/smoke-dequant-ptq1-arms.cljk \"$AMU\""]
  :doc "Bonsai stage C item 11 (ADR-0222): kernel-dequant-dot-ptq1-0 (kotoba-native ADR 0088) EXECUTED on both of its arms -- the legacy scalar arm under Rosetta 2 (no AVX) and the AVX2 arm on the x86_64 host PTQ1_AVX2_HOST names, over ssh -- each against kotoba.kir's C88A9DFA, with each arm broken separately in the machine code to show which machine ran which arm. Exit 2 when no AVX2 host is named (scalar measured, AVX2 not)."}

 :bonsai-qemu-admission
 {:cmd ["sh" "-c" "AIUEOS_QWEN35_ADMISSION_BONSAI=1 exec node \"${COM_JUNKAWASAKI_ROOT:-$HOME/github/com-junkawasaki}/scripts/resource-guard.mjs\" run build -- kbb --backend sci os/aiueos/scripts/smoke-qemu-qwen35-admission.cljk"]
  :doc "Bonsai stage A (ADR-0222): the three admission objects' Bonsai profile EXECUTED on a CPU. A real K16 qualification image boots under OVMF/QEMU (tcg), is handed the 11,120,992-byte real Bonsai prefix (bonsai-admission-fixture, via tests/make-bonsai-boot-fixture.cljk) through the model-handoff path, and must print QWEN-ADMIT reason=0 stage=0 admitted=1 and the tensor count, schedule, data offset, three representative offsets and artifact length that the fixture generator's receipt derived from the bytes. AIUEOS_QWEN35_ADMISSION_MUTATE=1 retypes token_embd.weight 143 -> 30 and requires reason=-21 stage=3. No prefix / no qemu is exit 3. ~3-4 min (build + boot)."}

 :bonsai-transport-qemu
 {:cmd ["sh" "-c" "set -eu; G=\"${COM_JUNKAWASAKI_ROOT:-$HOME/github/com-junkawasaki}/scripts/resource-guard.mjs\"; for p in bonsai2 qwen38; do AIUEOS_MODEL_PROFILE=$p node \"$G\" run build -- sh os/aiueos/scripts/smoke-qemu-model-handoff.sh; done; AIUEOS_MODEL_PROFILE=bonsai2 AIUEOS_MODEL_CORRUPT=1 node \"$G\" run build -- sh os/aiueos/scripts/smoke-qemu-model-handoff.sh"]
  :doc "Bonsai stage A item 5 (ADR-0222): the UEFI loader reads the model from a FAT32 split named by AIUEOS_MODEL_PROFILE -- bonsai2 is two files B2P0/B2P1 (production 4,000,000,000 + 1,946,648,928 = 5,946,648,928, sha256 53107f53...), qwen38 stays three Q38P0..2 -- into the one 2-MiB-aligned LoaderData mapping of ADR-0117, and the kernel maps it read-only/NX. QEMU/OVMF boots a byte-sized test-fixture split of each profile to AIUEOS_MODEL_HANDOFF_OK parts=2 / parts=3, and a one-byte-corrupt bonsai2 split is refused before kernel entry (code=121). The production-length Bonsai file has not been booted: that is the K16."}

