 :browser-desktop-focus-cycle
 {:cmd ["kbb" "--backend" "sci" "--classpath" "src" "scripts/compositor-guest.cljk" "guest-browser-focus-cycle"]
  :doc "Guest browser Alt+Tab (ADR-0237) on KERNEL.ELF under QEMU: after the pointer, the host opens window 2 from the launcher, then Alt down, Tab down / up three times, Alt up, a lone Tab. browser-key holds Alt in surface word 431 and answers 256 + the bottom window for each Tab under it; C hands the id to browser-reduce as :window/focus (kind 5), which raises it: stack 132 -> 321 -> 213 -> 132. Bodies unchanged, every census the frame model's. Tablet profile, 1260 s wall clock."}

 :browser-desktop-scroll
 {:cmd ["kbb" "--backend" "sci" "--classpath" "src" "scripts/compositor-guest.cljk" "guest-browser-scroll"]
  :doc "Guest browser wheel scroll (ADR-0238) on KERNEL.ELF under QEMU: after Alt+Tab, C registers app 4 (body: the lines 1 .. 20) and the host opens it from the launcher, sends a wheel notch over no window, moves to (300, 300), six notches down and seven up. C turns REL_WHEEL into tablet kind 6 / 7 and hands it to browser-reduce with the whole surface; the window under the pointer scrolls (browser.surface scroll-window, clamped at 0) by 20 px a notch, the offset in surface word 2039 + id, and browser-frame2 draws the body the offset higher, cut at the top inset. Offset 0 -> 120 -> 0; every census the frame model's. Tablet profile, 2400 s wall clock."}

 :browser-desktop-selection
 {:cmd ["kbb" "--backend" "sci" "--classpath" "src" "scripts/compositor-guest.cljk" "guest-browser-selection"]
  :doc "Guest browser selection (ADR-0240) on KERNEL.ELF under QEMU: after the wheel, the host sends five notches toward the end (window 4's offset to 100, line 20 inside it), then Shift down, Left, Left, Right, Left, Shift up, Backspace (each key down and up). browser-key holds Shift in surface word 2035 and runs browser.text-edit move-caret :extend? on the focused body -- the selection is the last k code points, words 2036 (window id) and 2037 (k) -- and delete-backward deletes it; browser-frame2 draws a #b5cdf1 highlight behind each selected glyph and no caret while something is selected (op capacity 259). k 0 -> 1 -> 2 -> 1 -> 2 -> deleted; every #111111 and #b5cdf1 census the frame model's. Tablet profile, 2700 s wall clock."}

 :browser-desktop-clipboard
 {:cmd ["kbb" "--backend" "sci" "--classpath" "src" "scripts/compositor-guest.cljk" "guest-browser-clipboard"]
  :doc "Guest browser clipboard (ADR-0241) on KERNEL.ELF under QEMU: after the selection, the host sends Shift, Left x3, Shift up, Ctrl, C, Ctrl up, Backspace, Ctrl, V x3, Ctrl up. browser-key holds Ctrl in surface word 2038 and answers Ctrl+C over a selection 512 (:clipboard/write) and Ctrl+V 513 (:clipboard/read), changing nothing; C asks broker-admit (ADR-0096) with the stage's grant (clipboard for events 1..19, file-picker only after) and hands the completion -- value 3, the 260-byte clipboard in place of the dictionary -- only on admit: copy \"19\\n\", delete, paste twice (45 -> 48 -> 51 code points), the refused third pastes nothing. Every census the frame model's. Tablet profile, 3000 s wall clock."}

 :browser-desktop-damage
 {:cmd ["kbb" "--backend" "sci" "--classpath" "src" "scripts/compositor-guest.cljk" "guest-browser-damage"]
  :doc "Guest browser damage (ADR-0242) on KERNEL.ELF under QEMU: every show of the desktop sends only the rectangle Kotoba browser-damage answers (the bounding box of every op, in the previous list or this one, at a slot where they differ) through virtio-gpu TRANSFER_TO_HOST_2D / RESOURCE_FLUSH. After the clipboard the host moves the tablet, then Alt, Tab (Alt+Tab raises window 1), Tab up, Alt up; after each the display is screendumped, F12 makes the kernel send the whole screen, and it is screendumped again. Green: the five rectangles are browser-frame-model.cljk's (300,300,32,22 / none / 80,80,652,716 / none / none) and every damage screendump is byte-identical to the whole-screen one after it; missing or stale screendumps are exit 3."}

