 :bonsai-rope-contract
 {:cmd ["sh" "-c" "ulimit -s 65520; node --stack-size=4000 \"$(command -v nbb)\" --classpath \"$(kbb -Spath -M:verify-admissions):../text/src\" os/aiueos/scripts/verify-admissions.cljk os/aiueos/contracts/qwen35-rope-v1.edn"]
  :doc "Bonsai stage B, the rope stage (ADR-0222 item 6): qwen35-rope executed in the KIR oracle against tests/prism_rope_oracle.c -- Prism llama.cpp 9a9394a's ggml_rope_cache_init + rotate_pairs verbatim with cosf/sinf replaced by the language's bounded sine/cosine: 15 vectors, 8 rotations (1 / 2 / 4 / 24 heads, positions 0 1 5 6 7 4096 15975 25735) and 7 refusals, reasons -4..0 all observed, 8 memory assertions over the WHOLE head (so a write past dimension 63 is caught). About 20 seconds."}

 :bonsai-rope-native
 {:cmd ["sh" "-c" "set -eu; AMU=${AMU:-../amu}; K=os/aiueos/kotoba; T=$(mktemp -d); \"$AMU/bin/amu\" compile $K/qwen35-rope.kotoba --target x86_64-aiueos-kernel-v1 --output $T/qwen35-rope.o --jvm-free > /dev/null; cmp $T/qwen35-rope.o $K/qwen35-rope.o; python3 os/aiueos/scripts/verify-kotoba-kernel-object.py $K/qwen35-rope.o \"\" kotoba_aiueos_qwen35_rope; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport struct\nb=open('os/aiueos/kotoba/qwen35-rope.o','rb').read()\nassert b'\\x41\\xff\\x91\\x90\\x00\\x00\\x00' not in b, 'slot-144 host call'\nfuel=struct.unpack_from('<I', b, 75)[0]\nassert fuel == 16777216, ('fuel word', fuel)\nprint('AIUEOS_BONSAI_ROPE_NATIVE_OK fuel=%d bytes=%d' % (fuel, len(b)))\nPY"]
  :doc "Bonsai stage B, the rope stage (ADR-0222): qwen35-rope COMPILES for x86_64-aiueos-kernel-v1 by the recipe reproduce-kotoba-objects.cljk records (`--jvm-free`, single file -- the `--unpinned --source-path` route compiles this source to DIFFERENT bytes, 6,232 vs 6,152, measured with amu f7e1bf4) with the pinned amu (needs amu's kotoba-native pin at a86c08c or newer: the kernel-object-entries row landed in kotoba-native #191; the previous pin refuses it by name, exit 70), is byte-identical to the committed .o, passes the ABI verifier under kotoba_aiueos_qwen35_rope with 0 imports, carries no slot-144 host call, and its packaged fuel word is the measured 16,777,216 tier. AMU defaults to ../amu."}

